{
  "_doc": {
    "about": "The composer's rich text (shared/src/compose/rich.ts, Android :core Rich.kt) and what typing markdown turns into in each editor (web: Tiptap, Android: Compose Rich Editor). Blocks are one per line: paragraph, heading (level), bullet, ordered (number), quote (each with runs: text, marks in the order bold, italic, strike, code, and href for links) or code (text with LF lines).",
    "markdown": "markdownToRich(markdown) with bare links (markdown typed elsewhere, as a signature) is `blocks`: a `[text](url)` only to an http, https or mailto address, its scheme in lower case; richToHtml(blocks) is `html` (compared after normalizeHtml), a link only to such an address; richToMarkdown(blocks) is `text`, the plain-text part, every link written out. Both editors load each `markdown` with bare links and hand back the same blocks.",
    "write": "richToMarkdown(blocks) is `text`, and markdownToRich(text) without bare links, as the composer reads back its own markdown, is `reread`: what the editors hold that markdown can't say as is; richToHtml(blocks) is `html` when given.",
    "typing": "`typed` typed into an empty editor, a key at a time, \"\\n\" as Enter; richToHtml of what the editor holds is `html` and richToMarkdown is `text`. `*bold*` takes one star and `_italic_` underscores; the rest are each library's own markdown shortcuts.",
    "links": "Link editing in each editor. `markdown` (one paragraph) is loaded and the selection set to `select`, offsets into the paragraph's text. The link button then opens the dialog for `dialog`: the link the selection starts in (`edit`, from just before its first letter to just after its last), else the selected text (`selection`), else a new link at the caret (`insert`), with the text and address it starts with. `remove` turns that link back into plain text; otherwise the dialog is saved with `text` and `href`. The editor then holds `expect` as markdown.",
    "plain": "plainLinks(markdown) is `text`, the plain-text part a draft or sent message carries: a link whose text is just its address (scheme http, https or mailto, a trailing slash and case aside) is written as that bare address where the line read back finds it there; other links stay `[text](url)`. draftLinks(text, the HTML markdownToHtml(markdown) without bare links writes) gives `markdown` back.",
    "draft": "draftLinks(text, html) is `markdown`: a reopened draft's plain-text part with its links taken from its HTML part (null for none). A bare address becomes `[address](url)`, with the link's own address, only where the HTML shows it as a link of just that text, counted in order among that address's appearances in each; links already written out stay."
  },
  "markdown": [
    {
      "name": "lines join with <br>, blank lines kept",
      "markdown": "Hello *world*\nsecond line\n\nNew paragraph",
